From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mirko Brombin <9479903+mirkobrombin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mm: take MTS references under page table locks without sleeping

Fork, zap and reclaim take and drop MTS references while holding PTE
spinlocks, but the reference table and the tier were guarded by mutexes, so
those paths slept in atomic context. The tier and reference locks become
spinlocks; provider I/O keeps its per-object mutex, which is now taken outside
the tier lock and revalidated against the generation. Allocating a new object
no longer sleeps under the tier lock.

install_mts_pte() returned on failure without ending the page walk, leaving
the PTE lock held: the next walk of that page spun forever. Fork cloned a
frozen object under both PTE locks; the clone now happens after they are
dropped and the copy retries. A stale reference failed fork through the swap
retry path, which loops on non-swap entries; it now fails with -ENOMEM.

---
--- a/mm/mts_tier.c
